## Final Judgement
## Summary

The evidence clearly demonstrates that Joe Biden explicitly and repeatedly denied wanting to ban fracking in the United States. Biden stated "I am not banning fracking. Let me say that again: I am not banning fracking" during a Pittsburgh speech, and in the very ABC News town hall video cited as the source of Charlie Kirk's claim, Biden said "I do not propose banning fracking." Biden's actual 2020 campaign platform did not call for a complete ban on all fracking—only for ending new fracking leases on federal land, which represents only 10% of all national leases. While Biden did make some statements during the Democratic primary debates (e.g., "no new fracking" and "we would make sure it's eliminated") that his campaign later clarified, his general election position was unambiguously against banning fracking. Fact-checking organizations characterized claims that Biden wanted to ban fracking as "repeated false claims."

